# 4. Create the Web Application

Create:

```text
web/index.html
```

Add:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Jenkins Docker CI/CD</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Hello from Jenkins + Docker!</h1>
    <p>This application was built and deployed using a Jenkins Pipeline.</p>

</body>
</html>
```

---

# 5. Create the Dockerfile

In the project root, create:

```text
Dockerfile
```

Add:

```dockerfile
FROM nginx:alpine

COPY web/index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html

EXPOSE 80
```

### Explanation

```dockerfile
FROM nginx:alpine
```

Uses a lightweight Nginx image.

```dockerfile
COPY web/index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
```

Copies our webpage into the Nginx web-server directory.

```dockerfile
EXPOSE 80
```

Documents that the application uses port 80 inside the container.

