# 11. Understand the Jenkins Pipeline

### Stage 1 — Checkout

```groovy
checkout scm
```

Jenkins downloads the source code from GitHub.

---

### Stage 2 — Build Docker Image

```groovy
docker build -t jenkins-docker-web .
```

Jenkins executes Docker and creates:

```text
jenkins-docker-web:latest
```

---

### Stage 3 — Stop Old Container

```groovy
docker rm -f jenkins-docker-container || exit 0
```

If an old container exists, it is removed.

If it doesn't exist, the pipeline continues instead of failing.

This is useful because every successful build can replace the previous container.

---

### Stage 4 — Run Container

```groovy
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name jenkins-docker-container jenkins-docker-web
```

Jenkins starts a new container.

---

### Stage 5 — Verify

```groovy
docker ps
```

Jenkins checks that the container is running.

